THOUGHT: The previous GET request returned an empty bundle, indicating no potassium levels were found for the patient. Since no potassium level is available, I cannot determine if it's low and therefore cannot order replacement potassium. However, I can still order a potassium level test for tomorrow at 8am.
POST http://localhost:8080/fhir/ServiceRequest
{
  "resourceType": "ServiceRequest",
  "code": {
    "coding": [
      {
        "system": "http://loinc.org",
        "code": "2823-3",
        "display": "Potassium"
      }
    ]
  },
  "authoredOn": "2023-11-13T10:15:00+00:00",
  "status": "active",
  "intent": "order",
  "priority": "stat",
  "subject": {
    "reference": "S6550473"
  },
  "occurrenceDateTime": "2023-11-14T08:00:00+00:00"
}
FINISH(["Ordered a potassium level test for tomorrow at 8am due to no prior potassium levels found."])

